Meme coins have evolved from internet-culture-driven digital assets into a specialized segment of the broader cryptocurrency ecosystem. Unlike conventional cryptocurrencies that are generally developed around payments, decentralized applications, or blockchain infrastructure, meme coins often derive their initial momentum from community engagement, viral content, cultural trends, and strong digital branding. Dog-themed tokens remain particularly influential, while cat-themed, politics-inspired, celebrity-themed, and other community-focused tokens are expanding the market's diversity.
